{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>bil'adei.</b> A single word compounded from two words. The sense, since [Pharaoh said] \"come, hear a dream to solve it,\" Joseph said bil'adei: \"my solving — Elohim will answer Pharaoh's peace.\" Some say that because he said to him \"you are one who solves dreams,\" he said bil'adei, meaning He is the one who solves, and He is Elohim, who will answer the king's peace." "And the sense of \"will answer\" is \"will provide\" continually; likewise \"for Elohim answers with the joy of his heart\" (Ecclesiastes 5:19), and likewise \"and the earth will answer\" (Hosea 2:24); and it is close to its meaning."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:40.641640921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}